# Files excluded from the archive uploaded to EAS Build.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAS uploads the repo ROOT (apps/mobile is a yarn workspace) and runs
#
#     yarn install --frozen-lockfile --production false
#
# in that root, which installs the dependencies of EVERY workspace it can see — not just the
# mobile app's. A workspace whose package.json is not in the archive is simply not a workspace on
# the builder, so its dependencies are never resolved, fetched, linked, or built.
#
# That is the whole mechanism: this file is the only lever that stops unrelated workspaces from
# being installed on an iOS/Android builder.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FAILURE THIS FIXES  (every iOS build errored from 2025-11-13 to 2026-08-16)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Expo build log — NOT the GitHub log, which only ever says "Unknown error, see the Install
# dependencies build phase" — showed, in phase INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES, step [5/5]:
#
#     error .../node_modules/@storybook/nextjs/node_modules/sharp,
#           .../node_modules/plasmo/node_modules/sharp: Command failed.
#     Command: node install/check
#     sharp: Detected globally-installed libvips v8.16.1
#     sharp: Attempting to build from source via node-gyp
#     ../metadata.cc:237:46: error: no member named 'NewOrCopy' in 'Napi::Buffer<char>'   (x5)
#     make: *** [Release/obj.target/sharp-darwin-arm64/metadata.o] Error 1
#
# The causal chain, verified end to end:
#
#   1. apps/extensions                                  -> plasmo@0.90.5           -> sharp 0.33.5
#      packages/toolkit/examples/next-boilerplate-ixartz -> @storybook/nextjs@8.6.18 -> sharp 0.33.5
#      Both land NESTED, because the repo root already hoists sharp 0.34.5.
#
#   2. The EAS macOS image (macos-sequoia-15.5-xcode-16.4) ships libvips 8.16.1 GLOBALLY.
#      sharp 0.33.5 declares `config.libvips: ">=8.15.3"`, and its install/check.js does:
#          if (useGlobalLibvips()) buildFromSource(...)
#      8.16.1 satisfies >=8.15.3, so sharp DELIBERATELY IGNORES its own prebuilt
#      @img/sharp-darwin-arm64 binary and compiles from source with node-gyp.
#      (Root sharp 0.34.5 escapes this only because it requires libvips >=8.17.3, which 8.16.1
#      does not satisfy — a margin of one minor release, not a design guarantee.)
#
#   3. apps/extensions -> plasmo -> @parcel/core -> lmdb -> node-addon-api ^4.3.0.
#      yarn 1 hoists that 4.3.0 copy to the ROOT node_modules. `Napi::Buffer<char>::NewOrCopy`
#      only exists from node-addon-api 6.x onward (verified: absent in 1.7.2 and 4.3.0, present
#      in 6.1.0, 7.1.1 and 8.5.0), so the source build fails to compile.
#
# So the browser extension and a Storybook example — neither of which a mobile binary has any use
# for — were together breaking every iOS build: one supplied the sharp that compiles, the other
# supplied the node-addon-api that cannot compile it.
#
# Excluding them removes BOTH halves. With the list below applied, the root node_modules hoists
# node-addon-api 6.1.0, and the only remaining native image dep is react-native-bootsplash's
# sharp 0.32.6, which compiles cleanly against it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THE LIST IS THIS BROAD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluding only the two guilty workspaces would fix today's failure and leave the trap armed:
# any workspace here may add a native or install-scripted dependency at any time and silently
# break iOS again, with a failure visible only in Expo's log. apps/mobile declares NO
# @ever-teams/* workspace dependency at all, so the required set is provably tiny:
#
#     apps/mobile              the app being built
#     packages/types           the root package.json devDepends on "@ever-teams/types": "*"
#     packages/eslint-config   packages/types devDepends on "@ever-teams/eslint-config": "*"
#
# Everything else is excluded. This is a GATE, not a removal: every workspace stays in the repo,
# in git, and in every other build. Only the mobile upload archive skips them.
#
# Verified before shipping, on the same toolchain the builder uses (yarn 1.22.22, node 24.14.0):
# with the 25 workspaces below removed, `yarn install --frozen-lockfile --production false`
# completes in 438s and exits 0. --frozen-lockfile fails on lockfile entries that are MISSING,
# never on ones that are merely unused, so extra yarn.lock entries are harmless.
#
# Defence in depth: apps/mobile/eas.json also sets SHARP_IGNORE_GLOBAL_LIBVIPS=1 on every build
# profile, which makes any sharp in the tree use its prebuilt binary instead of consulting the
# builder's global libvips. Keep both — this file stops the deps arriving, that flag stops any
# sharp that does arrive from compiling.
#
# Before adding a workspace back here, check what install scripts it drags onto a macOS builder.

apps/chatgpt
apps/extensions
apps/playground
apps/server-web
apps/storybook
apps/web
packages/api
packages/config-tailwind
packages/constants
packages/hooks
packages/services
packages/toolkit
packages/toolkit-types
packages/toolkit-ui
packages/ts-config
packages/ui
packages/utils
